WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.970
We started to predict this months ago when
it became clear that vote by mail or as I

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.730
am now calling it, absentee by mail voting
would be a huge dividing line in the upcoming

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.219
presidential election.

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:16.470
Also, don't forget, it will be a big deal
in the Senate, maybe remaining in Republican

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.359
control, maybe going to Democratic control.

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:25.119
They are going to be trying to stop vote by
mail and stop absentee voting.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.320
They're not even trying to hide it.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.630
I already told you that Donald Trump put a
donor of his named Lewis Dejoy in charge of

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.550
the post office as postmaster general.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:38.719
We suspected that Dejoy would try to hurt
the post offices ability to deliver mail.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:44.380
Dejoy has already limited overtime for mail
carriers, which is causing mail to pile up

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.719
at post offices across the country.

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:48.590
More cutbacks are now being discussed.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:55.269
But now the big breaking news is that Dejoy
has reassigned or fired more than two dozen

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:59.129
top postal officials specifically.

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:00.789
Two people have been removed.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:02.980
Twenty three have been reassigned.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.100
Anyone whose priorities are deliver, the mail
is being moved.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:14.820
And instead, Dejoy seems to be sort of centralizing
his power, consolidating the higher echelons

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.290
of the postal service with people that are
friendly to his truck, pro Trump priorities.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.060
And this is the mail that we're talking about.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:26.160
Ladies and gentlemen, if I had told you a
year ago the 2020 presidential election could

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.610
come down, not to the economy, not to Donald
Trump's foreign policy.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:35.180
It could come down to whether a Trump donor
succeeds at kneecapping and crippling the

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.180
post office.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.010
I don't think any of us would have believed
that that was a likely scenario.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.970
It's the scenario today and this is all having
an immediate effect.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.210
There are already many reports coming in from
around the country about mail delivery being

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.850
slowed down and degraded.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.640
There are reports of mail carriers having
to sort mail themselves something that's usually

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.060
done for them when they arrive and they're
ready to take out their mail for the day.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.130
It would already be sorted.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.680
They're having to sort it themselves, slows
them down even more.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.980
There are reports of mail bins that should
have been delivered already, sitting at post

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.250
offices unsorted and undelivered.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.830
And the sickest thing of it all.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:15.060
Is the backwards logic of everything, Trump
claimed that if there were too many absentee

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.500
ballots, the post office couldn't handle the
volume of mail.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:23.680
The post office said we can handle it just
fine unless you kneecap the post office, which

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.079
is exactly what they're doing.

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:30.879
They are making it so that the post office
will not be able to handle even the normal

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:32.650
mail delivery work.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.340
It's like a Trojan horse.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.340
You don't have to be.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.950
I hope you don't have to be anti Trump to
realize how evil this is.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:39.950
Right.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.340
I mean, will approach Trump.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.980
What will the pro trump people in my audience?

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.980
I know you're there.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.439
Will you come forward and say this is playing
dirty.

00:02:47.439 --> 00:02:48.599
This is anti-democratic.

00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:50.060
This has to be stopped.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.870
It's completely indefensible.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.900
And this they talk about election fraud.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.260
This should be called election fraud.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:04.180
So what can we do while we continue to sound
the alarm on this and demand that Dejoy be

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.190
trotted back to Congress to answer questions?

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:13.019
We have to just vote early, early, early,
or decide we feel safe enough to vote in person

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:15.730
depending on where you live.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:19.510
You within just weeks will be able to make
a vote by mail.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:24.569
If it gets delayed five days because of these
cuts, it'll still get there in plenty of time.

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:31.150
If you live in a state where you can believe
reasonably that you won't have to spend hours

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:36.840
in line with Marsalis people trying to vote,
maybe you decide, well, I'll vote in person

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.510
to ensure my vote is counted.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.829
In some places you will be waiting in line
for hours with people without masks and maybe

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:43.890
you don't want to do that.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.980
And it makes sense to just vote by mail as
early as you can.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.900
All of these problems are by design.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:53.989
We can't let them win at all, but we certainly
can't let them win like this.

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:58.810
Anyone who does not have a problem with this
is complicit in the eradication of democracy.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:04.569
In this case, being done through the proxy
of the U.S. Postal Service, Trump is realizing

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:07.730
the race is too uncertain unless he rigs it.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:13.290
As I said last week, Trump might be able to
win fair and square, although unlikely that

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.060
he would win the popular vote.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.560
He might be able to win the Electoral College
fair and square, maybe, but it's too close.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.610
It's too risky.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.450
And so they're pulling out all the stops.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:27.990
This is also, by the way, part of a bigger
Republican plan to get rid of government agencies

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:32.210
altogether, say that the United States Postal
Service is not up to the job.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:35.850
Then you cut their funding to prevent them
from being up to the job.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:39.100
Then you point to the problems you caused
to say, you know, we really should get rid

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.100
of that postal service.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.290
They're not doing a good job.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.340
Look at what they did during the 2020 election.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.720
We have to be on red alert because that's
exactly what this is.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:53.140
We'll have continued coverage of this on the
David Pakman show, Instagram at David Pakman

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.140
show.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.150
We'll take a quick break and be right back
after this.

